>
  <p><strong>No, GTA 6 doesn't have online multiplayer at launch.</strong> In its pre-order announcement Rockstar calls Grand Theft Auto VI "a single player experience" coming November 19, 2026. There's no online mode on day one, and no date has been announced for one.</p>

  <h2>What's confirmed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Launch is single-player:</strong> Jason and Lucia's story across the state of Leonida, on PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.</li>
    <li><strong>No online mode announced:</strong> Rockstar hasn't shared a name, date, player count or feature list for multiplayer.</li>
    <li><strong>In-game purchases exist:</strong> the ratings label lists "In-Game Purchases", and the Ultimate Edition Upgrade is sold as a separate add-on. That doesn't confirm an online mode.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="callout"><p>Seen claims of "32-player PvP" or "4-player co-op" on store pages and deal sites? Treat them as placeholder metadata. Rockstar hasn't announced either.</p></div>

  <h2>When could GTA 6 Online arrive?</h2>
  <p>Nobody outside Rockstar knows. Past launches offer a rough guide:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Game</th><th>Story launch</th><th>Online launch</th><th>Gap</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>GTA V</td><td>Sep 17, 2013</td><td>Oct 1, 2013 (GTA Online)</td><td>2 weeks</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Red Dead Redemption 2</td><td>Oct 26, 2018</td><td>Nov 27, 2018 (Red Dead Online beta)</td><td>~1 month</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GTA VI</td><td>Nov 19, 2026</td><td>Not announced</td><td>?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Both earlier online modes launched rough and took months to settle. If GTA 6 follows the pattern, expect online to arrive after launch, and expect it to be patchy at first.</p>

  <h2>Will GTA Online money transfer to GTA 6?</h2>
  <p>Nothing has been announced. Rockstar hasn't said anything about carrying over GTA Online cash, vehicles, properties or characters. The last generation jump (PS4 to PS5) let you migrate GTA Online progress into the new version of the same game. GTA 6 is a different game in a different state, so plan as if nothing carries over.</p>

  <h2>What happens to GTA Online?</h2>
  <p>It keeps going. No shutdown has been announced, weekly events are still rolling out, and GTA+ is still on sale. Until GTA 6 has its own online mode, GTA Online is still where Rockstar's multiplayer heists happen, and we track it every Thursday:</p>
